 "standard_url": "https://tea.texas.gov/about-tea/laws-and-rules/sboe-rules-tac/sboe-tac-currently-in-effect/ch111b.pdf",
 "standard_text": "2.7B use an understanding of place value to determine the number that is 10 or 100 more or less than a given number up to 1,200",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 2 worksheets for Texas TEKS 2.7B: count by 10s and 100s, find 10 more, 10 less, 100 more and 100 less up to 1,200, and number puzzles. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "10 more changes the tens; 100 more changes the hundreds.",
 "key_sub": "347 + 10 = 357. 347 + 100 = 447.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li><b>10 more</b> or <b>10 less</b> changes the <b>tens</b> digit by 1: 347 → 357 → 337.</li><li><b>100 more</b> or <b>100 less</b> changes the <b>hundreds</b> digit by 1: 347 → 447 → 247.</li><li>When the tens go past 9, regroup: 395 + 10 = 405.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>10 more than 496</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>9 tens + 1 ten = 10 tens</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Regroup to 5 hundreds</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 506</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>100 less than 1,082</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>1 thousand 0 hundreds → 9 hundreds</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 982</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Changing the ones digit</td><td>10 more changes the tens, not the ones.</td></tr><tr><td>Changing the wrong place</td><td>100 more changes the hundreds.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting to regroup</td><td>395 + 10 = 405, not 3,105.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does TEKS 2.7B ask?",
   "a": "Use an understanding of place value to determine the number that is 10 or 100 more or less than a given number up to 1,200."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do I need to count by ones?",
   "a": "No. Just change the tens or hundreds digit."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 10 more than 1,195?",
   "a": "1,205."
  },
  {
   "q": "How is 100 more like 10 more?",
   "a": "Both change one place by 1: the hundreds or the tens."
  }
 ],
